// Bech32 as the age format uses it: BIP 173's charset, checksum and letter
// case, without the ninety-character ceiling.
//
// BIP 173 caps a string at ninety characters because that is the largest a
// Bitcoin address needs, and the reference implementation enforces it. An age
// post-quantum public key is 1216 bytes, which is a 1974-character string, so
// the cap has to go: the checksum's guarantees do not depend on the length, and
// the format says so.
//
// It lives here, once, rather than in each key type that needs it; nothing
// outside this module can import it.
